#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:5
msgid "Groups"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:7
msgid "Groups gather members who share something: the board, a team, a section of your association, the people taking part in a project... A member can belong to as many groups as needed, and groups can be nested: a \"Juniors\" group can be placed under a \"Football\" group, for example."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:9
msgid "Each group can also have **managers**. A manager is a member who looks after the members of the group; what a manager is allowed to do is decided by the association, see :ref:`group managers <pref_rights>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:11
msgid "Groups are managed from **Management**, then **Groups**."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:14
#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:18
msgid "Groups list"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:16
msgid "The list displays all groups, the subgroups being placed under their parent group."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:23
msgid "**New group** creates a group: type its name and click on **Create**,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:24
msgid "**All groups PDF** exports all groups and their members in a single PDF file,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:25
msgid "the icons of the **Actions** column export the group as PDF, edit it, or delete it."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:27
msgid "To change the organisation of your groups, drag a group with the arrows icon and drop it under another one: it becomes its subgroup. Moving a group at the top of the list detaches it from its parent. Click on **Save** under the list to keep your changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:30
#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:34
msgid "Editing a group"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:32
msgid "Click on the edit icon of a group to see and change it."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:39
msgid "**Information**: the name of the group, and its **Parent group** if it is a subgroup,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:40
msgid "**Managers**: the members who manage the group. Click on **Manage managers** to add or remove some,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:41
msgid "**Members**: the members of the group. Click on **Manage members** to add or remove some."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:43
msgid "In both cases, a window opens with the list of members: click on a row to select a member, or to unselect them, then close the window. Do not forget to save the group afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:45
msgid "Groups can also be changed from a member card: the **Groups:** part of the member form lists the groups the member belongs to and the groups they manage."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:48
msgid "Several members at once"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:50
msgid "To add several members to a group, or to remove them from it, in one go:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:52
msgid "go to **Members**, then **List of members**, and select the members with the checkboxes,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:53
msgid "choose **Mass change** in the actions displayed under the list,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:54
msgid "in the **Groups:** part, pick a group in **Add to group** or in **Remove from group**,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:55
msgid "check the summary, and confirm."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:57
msgid "See :ref:`mass changes <mass_changes>` for the other information that can be changed this way."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:60
msgid "Deleting a group"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:62
msgid "Click on the delete icon of the group, and confirm. A group that still has members or subgroups cannot be deleted as is: check **Cascade delete** in the confirmation window to delete the group along with its subgroups. Members are never deleted; they are only removed from the group."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:65
msgid "Groups and searches"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/groups.rst:67
msgid "The members list can be filtered on a group, and the :ref:`advanced search <advsearch>` can find members belonging to several groups at once."
msgstr ""
